=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play ssh/legacy-v032 -----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
# Play mode, mocks: the SSH Login screen proposed for slice 6,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host (the SSH$
# checks, sshd.ReadEffective, migrate.Find, users.Read,$
# revert.ReadSession), each change the real steps.PlanSSH or$
# PlanMigration on the real plan/apply engine. The lockout$
# checks before asking are the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s$
# to build. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: ssh/legacy-v032$
# web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 26.04 (OpenSSH 10.2p1,$
# ssh.socket). Hardened by v0.3.2: its manage.conf, and$
# listen.conf for 2230 written with no daemon-reload, so$
# ssh.socket still listens on 22.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [?] SSH Port             Unknown socket and sshd differ$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Disallowed by manage.conf$
   -  Password Login       Off by 60-cloudimg-settings.conf$
   -  SSH Port             22, 2230 ssh.socket$
   -  Allowed Users        george by manage.conf$
  [ ] Old Settings         manage.conf, listen.conf$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Allow root key-only  Root logs in by key alone$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22 and 2230$
   4) Move old settings    Into 00-hardn.conf$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-4 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# hardn's old SSH files are still here (manage.conf,$
# listen.conf). Move them into 00-hardn.conf first: item 4.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [?] SSH Port             Unknown socket and sshd differ$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Disallowed by manage.conf$
   -  Password Login       Off by 60-cloudimg-settings.conf$
   -  SSH Port             22, 2230 ssh.socket$
   -  Allowed Users        george by manage.conf$
  [ ] Old Settings         manage.conf, listen.conf$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Allow root key-only  Root logs in by key alone$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22 and 2230$
   4) Move old settings    Into 00-hardn.conf$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-4 or q]: 4$
$
# Warning$
# /etc/systemd/system/ssh.socket.d/listen.conf (hardn v0.3.x)$
# sets ssh.socket to port 2230, but it never took effect:$
# ssh.socket is configured for [[::]:22 0.0.0.0:22] (no daemon-$
# reload since it was written, D9). Migrating it now could not$
# be rolled back: the rollback's daemon-reload would move$
# ssh.socket to port 2230 alone, off the port this host is$
# reached on (P-39). First make sure the firewall lets port 2230$
# through: ssh.socket then listens on port 2230 alone. Then let$
# listen.conf take effect while this session stays open: run$
# `systemctl daemon-reload` and `systemctl restart ssh.socket`$
# (established SSH sessions survive the restart), check that a$
# new SSH connection to port 2230 works, and run hardn again. A$
# reboot also lets it take effect, but ends this session: reboot$
# only with console access, in case port 2230 is not reachable.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [?] SSH Port             Unknown socket and sshd differ$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
